{
  "name": "Cheat sheet",
  "kind": "component",
  "component": "HottyKeys",
  "icon": "keyboard",
  "description": "Keys drawn as keycaps on their own, for a cheat sheet or an onboarding's keys: each chord a cap, a sequence's caps in order with > between them, alternatives apart by /, labelled for the user's system (mod+shift+p is Ctrl+Shift+P on Linux, ⌘⇧P on a Mac). A HottyKeys takes no focus and sends nothing: it shows keys and binds none. Each line is a Row of a HottyKeys and a Text weighted alike, so that the lines line up as a table's columns. The keys are bound to the data model, which the program writes from its keymaps: pick another Keymap and it sends the sheet that keymap's keys, after its leader (tmux's Ctrl+B, screen's Ctrl+A, Emacs's Ctrl+X).",
  "messages": [
